        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Reported abdominal and associated symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Central abdominal pain extending to peri-umbilical area and right iliac fossa for 4–5 days, ache 4–5/10, sometimes cramping after larger meals; mild nausea, no vomiting. Stools slightly looser for 3 days but still formed, 1–2 per day; no PR blood or melaena. No urinary symptoms or flank pain. No fevers, rigors, night sweats or weight loss. Appetite slightly reduced but still eating."
      }
